Sure! Below are the CSS and JavaScript codes that you can include in your HTML file. The CSS will handle the colors, while the JavaScript will add some interactivity using a simple script.

### CSS (styles.css)
```css
/* Import Google Font - Poppins */
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@400;500;600&display=swap');

* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
}

body {
    background: #f4f4f4;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding: 0 10px;
}

header {
    position: relative;
    background: #333;
    color: white;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 1em 0;
    width: 100%;
}

nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-around;
    background: #555;
    padding: 0.5em 0;
}

nav a {
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
}

section {
    margin: 2em 0;
}

footer {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 0;
    background: #333;
    color: white;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 1em 0;
    width: 100%;
}
```

### JavaScript (script.js)
```javascript
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function() {
    const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('nav a');
    navLinks.forEach(link => {
        link.addEventListener('mouseover', function() {
            this.style.color = '#ffcc00'; // Change color on hover
        });
        link.addEventListener('mouseout', function() {
            this.style.color = 'white'; // Revert to original color on mouse out
        });
    });
});
```

### HTML (index.html)
Here's how you can include the CSS and JavaScript files in your HTML:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Medical Firm</title>
    <!-- Link to the CSS file -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Medical Firm</h1>
    </header>
    <nav>
        <a href="#home">Home</a>
        <a href="#services">Services</a>
        <a href="#about">About Us</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>
    <section id="home">
        <h2>Welcome to Medical Firm</h2>
        <p>Providing quality healthcare services since 1995.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="services">
        <h2>Our Services</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>General Medicine</li>
            <li>Surgical Procedures</li>
            <li>Mental Health Counseling</li>
            <li>Emergency Care</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <section id="about">
        <h2>About Us</h2>
        <p>Medical Firm is dedicated to providing top-notch medical services. Our team of experts ensures that you receive the best care possible.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="contact">
        <h2>Contact Us</h2>
        <p>Email: info@medicalfirm.com</p>
        <p>Phone: 123-456-7890</p>
        <p>Address: 123 Medical St, Cityville, Country</p>
    </section>
    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2023 Medical Firm. All rights reserved.</p>
    </footer>

    <!-- Link to the JavaScript file -->
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

Make sure you have both `styles.css` and `script.js` files in the same directory as your HTML file, or adjust the paths accordingly. This setup will apply the styles defined in the CSS to your website and add some basic interactivity with JavaScript.
